|  1> # SCOPE 4  |  Tier 2 minima: B3LYP-D3(BJ)/def2-TZVP, TightOpt + FREQ
|  2> # State: V-I1 chemisorbed intermediate  |  register row: V-I1-T2-V02
|  3> # Start: TIER 1 accepted V-I1_canonical (Al four-coordinate, framework intact - the
|  4> #      self-correction recorded in the project memos).
|  5> # Why: this is the deep trap that makes the vanadium route thermodynamically distinct;
|  6> #      its Tier 2 energy is needed for the 188 kJ/mol chemisorption step.
|  7> # Expected: converges as a minimum, 0 imaginary modes.
|  8> # Gate: TERMINATED NORMALLY + 'THE OPTIMIZATION HAS CONVERGED' + 0 imaginary modes.
|  9> # Wall-time: the closest measured job (opt04 V-PRC, 30 atoms, 4 cores) took 9 h 52 m
| 10> #      for the optimisation alone; budget FREQ at 1.5-3x that. The 25-atom jobs are
| 11> #      roughly 3x cheaper. Run these before the OptTS jobs.
| 12> 
